  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CW: Partnership for Living Better: Affordable, Accessible, Adaptable Sanitation Solutions (LIXIL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Resilience and Food Security (RFS)):  Purpose: The purpose of the Partnership for Better Living activity, a collaboration between USAID and LIXIL Group&apos;s Safe Toilet (SATO) business unit, is to increase sustained household access to sanitation and increase adoption of key hygiene behaviors through market-based approaches. This activity will explore and expand upon USAID experience with market-based sanitation including contextual business models, supply chains, and public policies for introduction and expansion of sanitation products and services. This Activity aims to demonstrate how to partner effectively with a large multinational company within the sanitation value chain in USAID Water for the World High Priority and Strategy-Aligned Countries. The partnership aims to reach at least 2 million people, which by the end of year 5, will have toilets in their homes installed with affordable LIXIL SATO products...Activities: Through the Partnership for Better Living activity, USAID will collaborate with LIXIL to expand the market for affordable and appropriate sanitation solutions and improve the availability of products and reliability of supply chains in countries of shared interest, particularly in sub-Saharan Africa and Asia. Global and country level activities under this partnership and cooperative agreement will focus on: 1.) expanding the market and increasing demand for household sanitation products and services; 2.) improving the availability of products and reliability of supply chains; and 3.) supporting partnerships with other global and local sanitation stakeholders and advancing global knowledge of market-based solutions to sanitation challenges. USAID and LIXIL will identify up to 12 partnership priority countries at the planning stage and in consultation with Missions to meet demands for their bilateral sanitation and hygiene investments. .  .Benefitting Countries: (To be determined post-award)</narrative>
  </description>
